                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I’d like to give a mixed review, but since I can't, I'll give it thumbs down for all the backtracking. It’s a simple resource management game with 45 levels.\n\nPros\nIt has some nice artwork, and you can play through the levels without a timer. \n\nCons \nYou might have to restart the level if you make one mistake. This is especially frustrating because you might not realize the mistake until the end of the level. In addition, some levels require large stockpiles to solve them, so even if you don’t make any mistakes, you are stuck waiting until you can accumulate enough items to complete the level. Another flaw, there is not enough in-game explanation. For example, I had problems with level 8 because I ran out of stones for construction and I thought the market produced only gold. The market actually produces a random item so you will get stones if you wait long enough. However, there is absolutely no explanation provided and after getting gold three times in a row from the market, I had no reason to suspect that stones were forthcoming. \n",
